1
00:01:41,729 --> 00:01:48,870
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,430 --> 00:01:51,970
[Episode 14]

3
00:01:53,229 --> 00:01:54,479
Zhixia, let me tell you.

4
00:01:54,479 --> 00:01:56,400
You've come to the right person
for help picking out a new phone.

5
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,350
I know all the phones and models

6
00:01:57,350 --> 00:01:58,680
like the back of my hand.

7
00:01:59,000 --> 00:01:59,789
This one.

8
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:01,590
My idol is the spokesperson for it.

9
00:02:01,590 --> 00:02:02,560
It comes in 8 colors

10
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:03,920
and has 105 breathing light effects.

11
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:05,450
You can even customize
the light colors yourself.

12
00:02:05,450 --> 00:02:06,120
Isn't that cool?

13
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:09,199
[AISUN; 1999 yuan]

14
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:11,710
It's so pretty but a bit expensive.

15
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:13,090
It's over my budget.

16
00:02:17,079 --> 00:02:18,210
What about this one?

17
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:19,680
It's from a major brand

18
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,240
with a piano-finish coating,

19
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:23,040
and the price is reasonable too.

20
00:02:23,079 --> 00:02:24,340
This one is pretty too.

21
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:26,860
How about this one?

22
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:27,870
This one?

23
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:32,280
I've never even heard of this brand.

24
00:02:32,370 --> 00:02:34,520
-Is this some knockoff...
-Sis.

25
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:37,860
You have taste.

26
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,560
You really have great taste.

27
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:40,930
For all these years,

28
00:02:41,190 --> 00:02:42,520
I've been waiting for

29
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,930
someone who truly understands it.

30
00:02:47,079 --> 00:02:48,140
Understands what?

31
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:53,150
The Almighty King phone.

32
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,190
It's about to become

33
00:02:54,190 --> 00:02:56,450
the future leader of the phone industry.

34
00:02:57,590 --> 00:02:59,470
Its performance is insane—blazing fast!

35
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:01,240
And the battery life is unbelievable!

36
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:03,430
Normally, you only need to
charge it for 2 hours,

37
00:03:03,430 --> 00:03:05,150
and you can use it nonstop
for a whole week.

38
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:06,960
Plus, it's shockproof

39
00:03:07,630 --> 00:03:08,560
and waterproof.

40
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:13,150
Don't believe me?

41
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:25,280
See? Waterproof.

42
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:30,190
And that's not even the best part.

43
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:31,050
Watch closely!

44
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,900
Have you ever seen a phone this tough?

45
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,880
I just want to ask you—

46
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:41,420
have you ever seen a phone this tough?

47
00:03:41,590 --> 00:03:44,079
All-in-one, all-powerful.

48
00:03:44,310 --> 00:03:46,910
The Almighty King phone is trustworthy.

49
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,290
Choosing it is the right decision!

50
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:55,870
Sir, I don't need to
crack walnuts with it or anything.

51
00:03:55,870 --> 00:03:58,200
I just need it to
make calls and send texts.

52
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:00,360
The main thing is,
the price fits my budget.

53
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:02,290
I want to buy one for my brother too.

54
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:04,360
Sis, if you buy two today,

55
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,200
I'll give you a discount.

56
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,640
Are you sure? The Almighty King?

57
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:16,360
[Emile]

58
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:20,339
What are these?

59
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:24,220
We can afford 2 of these phones
within my budget.

60
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:25,680
Don't wait until after New Year's.

61
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:27,280
Let's share the good things.

62
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:32,630
These aren't...

63
00:04:33,159 --> 00:04:34,870
These aren't some knockoffs, are they?

64
00:04:34,870 --> 00:04:36,800
They're the Almighty King phones.

65
00:04:37,330 --> 00:04:40,300
Bet you didn't know that.
Not only do they have great performance,

66
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:42,030
but they're also built to last.

67
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:45,310
What you're really paying for
in an expensive phone is the brand value.

68
00:04:45,310 --> 00:04:47,110
I don't think that's necessary.

69
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:50,420
You really don't...

70
00:04:57,159 --> 00:04:57,950
Can they be returned?

71
00:04:57,950 --> 00:04:58,880
Why return them?

72
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:03,560
If you return them...
you can buy a more expensive one.

73
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:04,510
One you like more.

74
00:05:04,510 --> 00:05:06,310
Plus, I might get a new phone
for the New Year.

75
00:05:06,310 --> 00:05:08,970
I don't really need a phone
that badly right now.

76
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,750
But I picked these colors carefully.

77
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,240
Gold represents autumn,

78
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,840
and blue represents summer.

79
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:29,720
Since you don't like it, Brother,

80
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,300
I'll just return it.

81
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:33,800
Okay, okay, okay. I like it. I like it.

82
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:36,450
T-This is the Almighty King phone, right?

83
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,870
I've heard of this phone.

84
00:05:44,950 --> 00:05:46,550
It can really smash walnuts?

85
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:51,260
I'll smash it with yours then.

86
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:58,920
I-It's so sturdy.

87
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:16,830
Hello, Jiang.

88
00:06:16,950 --> 00:06:18,060
Guess who this is.

89
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:28,510
Hello?

90
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:30,090
Is it Lin Zhixia?

91
00:06:31,310 --> 00:06:32,870
How did you know it was me?

92
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:36,060
Didn't you ask me to guess?

93
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:37,659
I just guessed.

94
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,630
This is my number. Save it.

95
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:42,190
You're my best friend.

96
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:44,409
You're the first person I've told.

97
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,610
Let me tell you something amazing.

98
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,070
When I was choosing my phone number today,

99
00:06:50,070 --> 00:06:51,360
I saw one

100
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:52,950
where the last digits happened to

101
00:06:52,950 --> 00:06:54,630
match your birthday.

102
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,170
Isn't that amazing?

103
00:06:57,270 --> 00:07:00,350
[Answer]

104
00:06:59,070 --> 00:07:01,800
Too bad there wasn't one
ending with my birthday.

105
00:07:04,870 --> 00:07:06,680
That's a bit of a pity.

106
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:09,800
But it's already lucky enough, isn't it?

107
00:07:09,870 --> 00:07:12,130
And this number is very easy to remember.

108
00:07:13,190 --> 00:07:14,000
It's alright.

109
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:16,560
I remember other people's numbers too.

110
00:07:17,070 --> 00:07:19,000
So the contacts feature on your phone

111
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,530
is basically useless, huh?

112
00:07:23,190 --> 00:07:24,000
Lin Zhixia,

113
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,750
what name did you save me as?

114
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:30,070
Jiang Yubai.

115
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:34,750
Well, good friends

116
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:36,920
usually give each other nicknames—

117
00:07:36,950 --> 00:07:39,040
a name that only the two of them

118
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,000
would know.

119
00:07:45,310 --> 00:07:47,040
I'll have to think of a good one.

120
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,480
I gotta go.

121
00:07:50,630 --> 00:07:52,360
I need to call my other friends.

122
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:56,560
Alright then, bye-bye.

123
00:07:57,190 --> 00:07:57,920
Bye-bye.

124
00:08:03,610 --> 00:08:06,370
[Hang up]

125
00:08:15,410 --> 00:08:29,590
[Contacts: J-J-J-Jiang]

126
00:08:16,070 --> 00:08:16,870
Jiang...

127
00:08:29,310 --> 00:08:30,000
Son.

128
00:08:30,630 --> 00:08:31,600
Look at the time.

129
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:33,059
Why aren't you asleep yet?

130
00:08:33,549 --> 00:08:34,549
Mom, you're back.

131
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,120
Why are you home so late today?

132
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,549
Well, business has been busy lately,

133
00:08:37,549 --> 00:08:39,350
so I've had more client dinners.

134
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,320
But you.

135
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:41,600
Look at you.

136
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:44,380
Studying this late every day.

137
00:08:44,910 --> 00:08:47,640
You're not getting enough sleep.
That's no good.

138
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:49,320
Finals are coming up.

139
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,910
I need to prepare well.

140
00:08:52,550 --> 00:08:54,480
Your grades are already very good.

141
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:56,320
Don't push yourself so hard.

142
00:08:57,030 --> 00:08:57,870
That won't do.

143
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,080
Everyone else is working hard.

144
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,360
I can't afford to slack off.

145
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:02,560
I'm hoping to beat my previous ranking.

146
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,630
Look at you. You're already so tall,

147
00:09:06,630 --> 00:09:09,080
yet you still talk like a kid.

148
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:11,790
Other kids

149
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:14,080
need to be pushed and pushed to study.

150
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:15,390
But you?

151
00:09:15,630 --> 00:09:16,550
You're the opposite.

152
00:09:16,550 --> 00:09:18,200
I have to push you to rest.

153
00:09:20,550 --> 00:09:21,610
Alright, alright.

154
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:22,910
I won't nag you anymore.

155
00:09:22,910 --> 00:09:23,910
Go to sleep early.

156
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:28,840
Keep track of the time yourself, alright?

157
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:29,840
I know, Mom.

158
00:09:43,250 --> 00:09:44,200
Jiang...

159
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,120
You want to study me

160
00:09:55,530 --> 00:09:55,970
[The Human Observation Diary
is a preliminary research review]

161
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:58,080
because I am an ordinary human?

162
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:56,820
[on ordinary humans' thinking modes.]

163
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:58,920
That's right.

164
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,790
I feel like half of

165
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:03,620
my competitive streak was shaped by you.

166
00:10:06,750 --> 00:10:08,150
I will admit my mistakes and correct them.

167
00:10:08,150 --> 00:10:09,750
I'm apologizing to you right now.

168
00:10:09,750 --> 00:10:11,410
Jiang Yubai is not an ordinary human—

169
00:10:11,410 --> 00:10:13,840
he's a great genius.

170
00:10:17,150 --> 00:10:19,260
[Contacts; Name: No Ordinary Human]

171
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:41,080
[Contacts; Name: No Ordinary Human]

172
00:10:49,390 --> 00:10:52,190
[Astronomy Club]

173
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:08,870
Jin Baihui?

174
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,080
Hi.

175
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:11,010
You really came.

176
00:11:11,910 --> 00:11:13,120
Welcome to the astronomy club.

177
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:14,520
Feel free to look around.

178
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:38,170
What are you working on?

179
00:11:38,870 --> 00:11:40,390
I'm calibrating this dome.

180
00:11:40,390 --> 00:11:41,240
I want to watch

181
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:43,390
the meteor shower footage
we recorded earlier.

182
00:11:43,390 --> 00:11:44,150
A meteor shower?

183
00:11:44,150 --> 00:11:44,750
Yeah.

184
00:11:45,270 --> 00:11:46,730
Want to watch it together?

185
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:47,910
Sure.

186
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:51,040
This meteor shower happened

187
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:53,250
around 10:30 PM the night before last.

188
00:11:54,630 --> 00:11:57,080
First, there was a partial lunar eclipse,

189
00:11:58,240 --> 00:12:00,000
then the meteor shower reached its peak.

190
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:00,750
Have a seat.

191
00:12:02,150 --> 00:12:04,910
In the end, they formed a rare phenomenon:

192
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:08,480
an eclipsed moonrise
accompanied by a meteor shower.

193
00:12:09,650 --> 00:12:11,440
Since this dome is a simulator,

194
00:12:11,970 --> 00:12:14,970
seeing it in person
would've been even more stunning.

195
00:12:22,270 --> 00:12:23,800
Where is the meteor shower?

196
00:12:24,070 --> 00:12:25,000
Wait a moment.

197
00:12:33,630 --> 00:12:34,360
I see it.

198
00:12:49,790 --> 00:12:50,990
Are you making a wish?

199
00:13:11,670 --> 00:13:13,470
Why did the meteors stop moving?

200
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:15,180
Weren't you making a wish?

201
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:16,380
I paused it for you.

202
00:13:50,870 --> 00:13:52,120
If there's nothing else,

203
00:13:51,850 --> 00:13:54,340
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

204
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:53,990
that's all for today.

205
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:01,000
Let me say a few more things.

206
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,400
Put down your pens first.

207
00:14:04,150 --> 00:14:05,150
Our experimental class

208
00:14:05,150 --> 00:14:07,120
is the best group of students
in the entire grade.

209
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:08,580
There is no doubt about it.

210
00:14:08,910 --> 00:14:10,630
So you've already gotten used to

211
00:14:10,630 --> 00:14:11,890
being praised as smart

212
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:13,480
and getting better grades
on your report cards

213
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,440
than everyone else.

214
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:15,150
But...

215
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:19,030
the final exams can't be handled
on autopilot.

216
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,150
The subjects you feel most confident in

217
00:14:22,150 --> 00:14:24,150
might be where others overtake you.

218
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:27,420
The questions you think you got right

219
00:14:27,510 --> 00:14:29,200
may be the very ones that drag down

220
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:30,200
your ranking.

221
00:14:30,910 --> 00:14:34,480
So being in the experimental class
is not a free pass.

222
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:37,200
You have to be more careful than ever.

223
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:41,510
Also, our class has
the rank-based elimination system.

224
00:14:41,510 --> 00:14:43,030
If the sum of your two exam scores

225
00:14:43,030 --> 00:14:46,120
falls out of the top 50 in the grade,
you'll automatically be transferred out.

226
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:47,120
You all know this.

227
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:49,250
When that happens, no one can help you.

228
00:14:49,390 --> 00:14:51,200
So, with the holiday coming up soon,

229
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,910
I don't want the exam results

230
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,320
to ruin your New Year.

231
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:58,750
So do your best
and take the exams seriously, okay?

232
00:14:58,750 --> 00:14:59,390
Okay.

233
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,320
Okay.

234
00:15:00,340 --> 00:15:00,950
Okay.

235
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:01,410
Okay.

236
00:15:01,510 --> 00:15:02,840
Louder. Okay?

237
00:15:02,870 --> 00:15:04,200
Okay!

238
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:05,950
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

239
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:05,080
Do your best.

240
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,680
Good luck. Don't be nervous.

241
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:14,530
Brother, what's for dinner today?

242
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:18,750
Not at home?

243
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:48,920
How did this book end up with you?

244
00:15:51,270 --> 00:15:54,840
Jin Baihui came over
and returned this book a few days ago.

245
00:15:56,670 --> 00:15:58,120
Her dad tore it up.

246
00:15:58,720 --> 00:15:59,510
Why?

247
00:16:04,750 --> 00:16:06,670
She didn't do well
on her last monthly exam.

248
00:16:06,670 --> 00:16:09,480
Her dad thought
she wasn't focusing on her studies.

249
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,150
So giving her this book was your way of

250
00:16:11,150 --> 00:16:13,010
intentionally distracting her.

251
00:16:13,150 --> 00:16:14,440
What do you mean she didn't do well?

252
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:16,150
She's still in the top few in the grade

253
00:16:16,150 --> 00:16:18,240
and has always studied hard.

254
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:20,630
In her parents' eyes—

255
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:23,180
actually, in many people's eyes—

256
00:16:23,790 --> 00:16:25,250
if you don't come in first,

257
00:16:25,910 --> 00:16:27,310
that's a failure in life.

258
00:16:28,610 --> 00:16:29,670
Tearing up the book

259
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:32,280
is just an extreme way of expressing it.

260
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:36,210
Is being first really that important?

261
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:38,550
Jiang Yubai had always wanted to beat me

262
00:16:38,550 --> 00:16:39,750
and come in first too.

263
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,730
But grades aren't everything.

264
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:46,000
Only people...

265
00:16:48,670 --> 00:16:52,130
who've actually gotten first place
have the right to say that.

266
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,660
Anyway, don't worry about it.

267
00:16:59,790 --> 00:17:01,630
And don't tell Jin Baihui either.

268
00:17:01,630 --> 00:17:03,360
She already feels bad about it.

269
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:11,280
Ten minutes left until the exam ends.

270
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:13,319
Please manage your time.

271
00:17:54,790 --> 00:17:55,720
I did pretty well.

272
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:56,440
Yeah.

273
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:57,030
Let's go.

274
00:17:57,030 --> 00:17:57,680
Let's go.

275
00:18:13,590 --> 00:18:15,190
I was careless. So careless.

276
00:18:15,550 --> 00:18:17,000
I should've gotten full marks
on my combined science.

277
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,480
God knows what obscure detail
cost me 2 points.

278
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:20,310
Shen,

279
00:18:21,030 --> 00:18:22,550
if I hadn't made a careless mistake,

280
00:18:22,550 --> 00:18:24,350
you wouldn't have caught up with me.

281
00:18:24,350 --> 00:18:26,400
Then you'd better be careful next time.

282
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:27,860
After all, the same excuse

283
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:29,310
won't work twice.

284
00:18:32,150 --> 00:18:32,750
By the way,

285
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:33,550
I heard

286
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:37,240
those starch sausages
aren't good for your brain.

287
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:38,830
Give me a break.

288
00:18:41,310 --> 00:18:43,200
Lin Zhixia actually
didn't get first place?

289
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:44,600
That doesn't seem right.

290
00:18:45,590 --> 00:18:48,120
Could it be
that everything happening lately

291
00:18:48,350 --> 00:18:49,350
distracted her?

292
00:18:51,110 --> 00:18:53,110
But she shouldn't have dropped to fifth.

293
00:18:53,110 --> 00:18:55,310
I'm only 4 places behind Lin Zhixia?

294
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:57,440
This is so encouraging!

295
00:18:58,580 --> 00:18:59,510
What about Tang?

296
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:05,680
Our dead last, Tang Tingting.

297
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:06,830
She's always been consistent.

298
00:19:06,830 --> 00:19:08,560
She dropped a few places again.

299
00:19:11,750 --> 00:19:12,400
Let's go.

300
00:19:12,830 --> 00:19:13,400
Go.

301
00:19:27,750 --> 00:19:28,810
Congratulations.

302
00:19:29,110 --> 00:19:29,920
You did great.

303
00:19:31,930 --> 00:19:32,980
[Grade 10 Final Exam Rankings]

304
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:33,740
[1; Jin Baihui] [2; Jiang Yubai]

305
00:19:33,770 --> 00:19:34,670
[3; Zhao Li] [4; Li Yuanyuan]

306
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:35,990
[5; Lin Zhixia] [6; Wang Xinrui]

307
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:46,690
The formula
must have been written incorrectly.

308
00:19:49,290 --> 00:19:50,880
Why were 2 points deducted?

309
00:20:05,640 --> 00:20:07,400
Tang, you're really bad at
science subjects.

310
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,510
Especially math.

311
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:11,570
I could score higher than you
with my eyes closed.

312
00:20:11,570 --> 00:20:12,270
Get lost.

313
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,800
I'm not in the mood to talk to you.

314
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:22,720
Lin Zhixia,

315
00:20:22,830 --> 00:20:24,270
can I borrow your math paper

316
00:20:24,270 --> 00:20:25,400
to check my answers?

317
00:20:28,270 --> 00:20:28,960
Thanks.

318
00:20:36,830 --> 00:20:39,030
So that's what the last question meant.

319
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:41,480
I didn't even understand it before.

320
00:20:43,830 --> 00:20:44,720
Wait a minute.

321
00:20:45,590 --> 00:20:47,310
You got
all the long-answer questions right.

322
00:20:47,310 --> 00:20:49,040
Then where did you lose points?

323
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:57,830
How did you get this question wrong?

324
00:20:57,830 --> 00:20:58,890
Even I got it right.

325
00:20:59,350 --> 00:21:00,160
And this one.

326
00:21:03,940 --> 00:21:05,270
I... I... well...

327
00:21:07,310 --> 00:21:09,400
I-I lost focus during the exam.

328
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:13,960
Thanks.

329
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:51,920
Lin Zhixia.

330
00:21:53,790 --> 00:21:54,850
Why did you do this?

331
00:21:57,040 --> 00:21:57,880
What's wrong?

332
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:01,720
Math is your strongest subject.

333
00:22:02,510 --> 00:22:06,440
There's no way you'd get the first 2
multiple-choice questions wrong.

334
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:09,780
You did it on purpose, didn't you?

335
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:11,030
I didn't.

336
00:22:20,060 --> 00:22:21,350
Do you think you have to hold back

337
00:22:21,350 --> 00:22:22,310
for me to win?

338
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,480
Are you taking pity on me?

339
00:22:25,830 --> 00:22:27,160
Do you think I'm stupid?

340
00:22:29,510 --> 00:22:30,640
During this whole final exam period,

341
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:32,970
I studied until after midnight every day.

342
00:22:33,750 --> 00:22:36,080
And yet, what I won
was a fake competition.

343
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:40,030
I don't study for exam rankings...

344
00:22:40,030 --> 00:22:40,830
I do!

345
00:22:45,110 --> 00:22:45,880
Okay?

346
00:22:47,010 --> 00:22:52,930
[Toward a Sea of Stars,
Chasing Our Dreams]

347
00:22:56,840 --> 00:23:01,810
[Toward a Sea of Stars,
Chasing Our Dreams]

348
00:23:28,110 --> 00:23:30,400
Come on. Open your books to page 67.

349
00:23:35,420 --> 00:23:37,060
[A hundred-year undertaking
begins with education]

350
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:09,060
What are you doing?

351
00:24:10,510 --> 00:24:11,680
I'm observing you.

352
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:13,750
I'm planning to write

353
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:16,180
a Human Observation Diary about you too.

354
00:24:17,070 --> 00:24:18,600
And what have you observed?

355
00:24:19,830 --> 00:24:20,720
I've observed

356
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:22,310
that Lin Zhixia has

357
00:24:22,590 --> 00:24:24,790
taken a little detour on her way

358
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:27,340
to becoming more emotionally intelligent.

359
00:24:28,510 --> 00:24:30,770
To help her friend improve her rankings,

360
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:33,750
she deliberately held back on the exams.

361
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:36,240
But because of her clumsy tricks,

362
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:37,500
she gave herself away.

363
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:43,440
I thought I was helping Jin Baihui.

364
00:24:44,310 --> 00:24:47,000
But I can't understand why she got angry.

365
00:24:50,530 --> 00:24:51,990
You know what, Lin Zhixia?

366
00:24:52,790 --> 00:24:53,850
Although this time

367
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:56,590
you deliberately held back
so I could outrank you,

368
00:24:56,590 --> 00:24:57,350
to me,

369
00:24:57,350 --> 00:24:59,550
this isn't something to be happy about.

370
00:25:02,310 --> 00:25:04,370
I think Jin Baihui feels the same way.

371
00:25:07,030 --> 00:25:09,430
She didn't do well
on the last monthly exam.

372
00:25:10,110 --> 00:25:13,350
Maybe she spent this entire month
studying harder than ever.

373
00:25:13,350 --> 00:25:15,200
Every time she felt like
she couldn't keep going,

374
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:16,440
she probably thought,

375
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:17,400
"Maybe if I try a little harder,

376
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:18,860
I can surpass Lin Zhixia."

377
00:25:19,110 --> 00:25:20,720
And she'd be motivated again.

378
00:25:20,720 --> 00:25:22,520
But she never saw you as an enemy,

379
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:24,480
only as an opponent.

380
00:25:29,590 --> 00:25:33,070
That's a form of admiration,
recognition, and respect.

381
00:25:37,590 --> 00:25:39,320
Just like in a basketball game.

382
00:25:39,350 --> 00:25:42,150
Whenever the ace players
from both sides face off,

383
00:25:42,160 --> 00:25:43,890
the audience stands and cheers

384
00:25:44,270 --> 00:25:46,000
because everyone expects

385
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:47,460
a true, all-out showdown.

386
00:25:48,510 --> 00:25:49,680
No matter who wins or loses,

387
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:52,010
the players exchange jerseys afterward.

388
00:25:52,480 --> 00:25:54,350
It's a truly wonderful moment.

389
00:26:00,640 --> 00:26:01,480
It's like...

390
00:26:02,750 --> 00:26:04,200
you've prepared yourself

391
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:06,200
extremely thoroughly for a match,

392
00:26:06,550 --> 00:26:08,680
but your opponent suddenly forfeits.

393
00:26:08,830 --> 00:26:10,360
Would you still feel happy?

394
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:46,920
This is the latest math practice test

395
00:26:46,920 --> 00:26:48,480
based on the Grade 10 curriculum,

396
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:50,030
available in bookstores.

397
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:53,240
Jin Baihui,

398
00:26:53,830 --> 00:26:54,830
I'd like to invite you

399
00:26:54,830 --> 00:26:57,490
to compete with me again
during the lunch break.

400
00:26:58,440 --> 00:26:59,200
I promise

401
00:26:59,640 --> 00:27:01,240
I'll give it my all this time.

402
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:20,750
Then eat faster,

403
00:27:20,920 --> 00:27:23,180
or we won't have enough time for the test.

404
00:27:28,280 --> 00:27:32,100
[Pursue Knowledge, Seek Truth;
Practice Diligently, Foster Innovation]

405
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:29,830
Lin Zhixia,

406
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:32,010
do your best this time.

407
00:27:32,680 --> 00:27:34,510
Don't worry. I won't hold back.

408
00:27:42,530 --> 00:27:46,920
[VS]

409
00:27:46,780 --> 00:27:49,940
♪ The world is limitless colour puzzle ♪

410
00:27:50,210 --> 00:27:53,340
♪ I have the wildest dreams;
never fitting in ♪

411
00:27:53,790 --> 00:27:56,680
♪ The formula in my mind
is messed up and reorganized ♪

412
00:27:57,270 --> 00:28:00,270
♪ Is loneliness my only talent? ♪

413
00:28:00,940 --> 00:28:04,610
♪ Hide in the midsummer tree shade;
what's waiting for my answer? ♪

414
00:28:04,970 --> 00:28:07,040
♪ The breeze blows past my cheeks ♪

415
00:28:07,860 --> 00:28:10,660
♪ How do I solve for
the unexpected variables? ♪

416
00:28:11,100 --> 00:28:13,880
♪ At the most splendid moment ♪

417
00:28:14,610 --> 00:28:17,730
♪ Running and waiting for my exploration ♪

418
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:20,920
♪ The unknown is so fascinating ♪

419
00:28:21,430 --> 00:28:23,600
♪ Young me stood on tiptoes ♪

420
00:28:24,070 --> 00:28:28,050
♪ Everything is transparent;
time is too light ♪

421
00:28:28,790 --> 00:28:29,270
♪ Natural deduction ♪

422
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:31,520
I think I did even better
than on the final exam.

423
00:28:31,550 --> 00:28:32,350
Me too.

424
00:29:13,070 --> 00:29:18,280
[Pursue Knowledge, Seek Truth;
Practice Diligently, Foster Innovation]

425
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:34,140
Jin Baihui's score is out.

426
00:29:35,140 --> 00:29:37,000
-How many points did she get?
-What's her score?

427
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:37,770
No way.

428
00:29:38,110 --> 00:29:39,310
148?

429
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:40,590
148.

430
00:29:40,750 --> 00:29:42,640
That's 2 points higher
than her final exam score.

431
00:29:42,640 --> 00:29:43,400
Yeah.

432
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:44,590
So impressive.

433
00:29:44,830 --> 00:29:46,000
-She only missed one fill-in-the-blank.
-So impressive.

434
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:47,310
That's incredible.

435
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:49,220
What about Lin Zhixia?

436
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:51,660
Lin Zhixia's score is out too.

437
00:30:11,680 --> 00:30:12,590
First place.

438
00:30:13,270 --> 00:30:15,350
Baihui, you did really well this time.

439
00:30:15,350 --> 00:30:17,070
Your hard work paid off.

440
00:30:17,310 --> 00:30:19,310
Hard work always pays off, you know?

441
00:30:19,880 --> 00:30:20,550
See?

442
00:30:20,550 --> 00:30:22,240
Mom and Dad were right to stop you from

443
00:30:22,240 --> 00:30:23,350
wasting time on those useless

444
00:30:23,350 --> 00:30:24,160
extracurricular activities.

445
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:26,310
Otherwise, how could you have achieved
such a great ranking?

446
00:30:26,310 --> 00:30:27,550
I think she lost 5 points in Chinese

447
00:30:27,550 --> 00:30:29,480
because of her essay.

448
00:30:29,480 --> 00:30:30,980
These 4 points off in math...

449
00:30:30,980 --> 00:30:33,510
Actually, I didn't get
first place this time.

450
00:30:35,790 --> 00:30:36,720
What do you mean?

451
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:37,830
What happened?

452
00:30:40,310 --> 00:30:41,310
Lin Zhixia let me

453
00:30:41,740 --> 00:30:43,270
take first place this time.

454
00:30:44,590 --> 00:30:45,450
Let you take it?

455
00:30:49,830 --> 00:30:52,200
Are you still happy now?

456
00:30:58,750 --> 00:31:00,950
What's the point of being first anyway?

457
00:31:00,960 --> 00:31:01,960
What's the point?

458
00:31:03,270 --> 00:31:05,400
In this society, except for first place,

459
00:31:05,400 --> 00:31:07,510
second place is
no different from last place.

460
00:31:07,510 --> 00:31:09,400
In a competition,
the runner-up is just a loser.

461
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:10,640
Don't you understand that?

462
00:31:10,640 --> 00:31:12,000
But does that mean
all the effort a runner-up puts in

463
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:12,880
is just a waste?

464
00:31:12,880 --> 00:31:15,030
The college entrance exam
only cares about the result.

465
00:31:15,030 --> 00:31:16,160
For that result,

466
00:31:16,160 --> 00:31:18,350
your dad and I
have kept making sacrifices.

467
00:31:18,350 --> 00:31:19,310
Back then, for you...

468
00:31:19,310 --> 00:31:19,960
Yes!

469
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:22,790
Back then, you gave up your jobs

470
00:31:22,790 --> 00:31:24,310
to accompany me to Beijing.

471
00:31:24,310 --> 00:31:25,350
When I couldn't keep up
in the gifted class,

472
00:31:25,350 --> 00:31:26,350
you came back with me.

473
00:31:26,350 --> 00:31:27,640
I know that.

474
00:31:28,350 --> 00:31:29,680
I'm very grateful.

475
00:31:31,030 --> 00:31:33,350
But I gave it my absolute all back then.

476
00:31:35,270 --> 00:31:36,920
I slept less than 5 hours a day

477
00:31:36,920 --> 00:31:39,520
and spent the rest of my time
doing test papers.

478
00:31:40,110 --> 00:31:41,440
I felt like I was close to

479
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:43,570
breaking down mentally back then.

480
00:31:44,160 --> 00:31:46,000
But why did you still keep pushing me?

481
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:47,790
You two are ordinary people too!

482
00:31:47,790 --> 00:31:49,640
Baihui, who was pushing you?

483
00:31:49,830 --> 00:31:53,030
I try my hardest every single day,
every single moment.

484
00:31:53,440 --> 00:31:55,550
But everyone's limit is different.

485
00:31:57,200 --> 00:31:59,330
After I found out Lin Zhixia let me win,

486
00:32:00,030 --> 00:32:01,760
I even competed with her again.

487
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:02,830
And the result?

488
00:32:05,440 --> 00:32:06,440
I just lost.

489
00:32:07,350 --> 00:32:08,680
She got a perfect score.

490
00:32:10,110 --> 00:32:11,640
But so what?

491
00:32:13,270 --> 00:32:15,030
At No. 1 High School, there's Lin Zhixia—

492
00:32:15,030 --> 00:32:16,550
and in this world, there are

493
00:32:16,550 --> 00:32:18,440
countless more people
who are even better than Lin Zhixia.

494
00:32:18,440 --> 00:32:20,370
When does the comparing ever stop?

495
00:32:29,180 --> 00:32:29,830
Dad.

496
00:32:31,510 --> 00:32:32,200
Mom.

497
00:32:34,350 --> 00:32:36,210
You probably didn't even notice—

498
00:32:37,440 --> 00:32:38,440
this time I scored

499
00:32:39,480 --> 00:32:41,610
a full 20 points higher than last time.

500
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:45,060
Every single point

501
00:32:46,250 --> 00:32:48,720
was earned with all my effort.

502
00:32:56,960 --> 00:32:58,070
So from now on...

503
00:33:00,290 --> 00:33:02,020
I'll only compete with myself.

504
00:33:24,250 --> 00:33:26,380
[Grade 10 Math
Semester 1 Required Module 1]

505
00:33:26,400 --> 00:33:28,640
[Comprehensive Test; Total Mock Test; 3]

506
00:33:30,320 --> 00:33:32,220
Now, I can't even remember

507
00:33:33,290 --> 00:33:36,080
[Grade 10 Math
Semester 1 Required Module 1]

508
00:33:33,460 --> 00:33:35,900
what mindset I had back then

509
00:33:36,100 --> 00:33:38,160
[Comprehensive Test; Total Mock Test; 3]

510
00:33:36,310 --> 00:33:39,710
when I deliberately got
2 multiple-choice questions wrong.

511
00:33:39,790 --> 00:33:41,510
I think I simply felt

512
00:33:42,180 --> 00:33:44,640
that Jin Baihui was
under too much pressure.

513
00:33:46,090 --> 00:33:47,090
In the rematch,

514
00:33:47,880 --> 00:33:48,790
she lost to me—

515
00:33:49,940 --> 00:33:51,870
but that gave her more peace of mind

516
00:33:52,220 --> 00:33:54,280
than winning first place would have.

517
00:33:54,880 --> 00:33:56,340
It also made me understand

518
00:33:57,550 --> 00:33:58,610
that true respect

519
00:33:59,030 --> 00:34:03,970
[Jin Baihui] [Lin Zhixia]

520
00:33:59,250 --> 00:34:00,450
is not about yielding

521
00:34:01,310 --> 00:34:03,570
but going all out when facing each other.

522
00:34:05,530 --> 00:34:06,610
Fortunately,

523
00:34:07,610 --> 00:34:10,210
my little scheme—smart or not—
finally helped

524
00:34:10,460 --> 00:34:13,190
Jin Baihui let go of
what had been weighing on her.

525
00:34:14,770 --> 00:34:15,820
From then on,

526
00:34:16,500 --> 00:34:17,690
her biggest rival

527
00:34:17,820 --> 00:34:18,760
was no longer me,

528
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:21,360
but her past self.

529
00:34:21,179 --> 00:34:27,840
[Contacts: L-L-L-L-Lin Zhixia]

530
00:34:27,870 --> 00:34:33,600
[Contacts: High-EQ Human]

531
00:34:49,949 --> 00:34:53,199
[Go All Out, Friendship Forever]
